#
# An aggregator that is ITSELF named `manifest.ttl`. This is the double-count
# shape: `crates/sparql-conformance/tests/sparql_conformance.rs` runs every
# `manifest.ttl` below `suite/` as a case, so it would discover this file AND the `manifest.ttl`
# files it includes — and every included case would run twice, once directly and
# once through here, silently doubling the pass tally.
#
# `manifest::load` refuses it by name. An aggregator must be named something
# discovery does not match, as the vendored SEP-0009 corpus's `manifest-all.ttl`
# is, which makes group discovery and aggregation disjoint by construction rather
# than by accident of one file's name.
@prefix mf: <http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/test-manifest#> .

<> a mf:Manifest ;
    mf:include ( <group/manifest.ttl> ) .
